{
  "company_name": "PowerLedger Corp",
  "industry": "Power Generation",
  "use_case": "Power generation financial analytics and budget reporting",
  "space_title": "PowerLedger Corp - Financial Analytics & Reporting 💰",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Power Generation\n\n**Use case:** Financial Analytics & Budget Reporting\n\nPowerLedger Corp — fleet financial analytics across 20 cost centers spanning generation, fuel, maintenance, and corporate departments. The CFO, FP&A leads, and department heads use this space to track revenue, budget variance, and operating margin; the Treasury and Capex governance teams use it to monitor capital commitment, YTD spend pacing, and approval-status backlog.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Total revenue (USD) — top-line by department and quarter\n- Actual vs. budget variance ($, %) — favorable/unfavorable flag\n- Operating margin (%) — utility-sector benchmark ~12-18%\n- YTD spend pacing vs. annual budget — burn-rate indicator\n- CapEx committed (USD) — capital governance metric\n- Budget status distribution — On Track / At Risk / Over Budget\n- Cost per MWh (derived) — fleet-wide efficiency view\n- Approval status backlog — Pending vs Approved transaction count\n\n**Data sources**\n- `cost_centers` — daily expense transactions with category, line item, approval status\n- `financial_transactions` — period revenue, actual cost, budget cost, variance by cost center\n- `budget_snapshots` — annual budget, YTD spend, remaining budget, capex committed, margin, status",
  "schema_basename": "power_financial_analytics",
  "tables": [
